{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "20047",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.71,
      "end_seconds": 5.36,
      "duration_seconds": 4.65,
      "text": "Hi, is it okay to come in now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.87,
      "end_seconds": 10.28,
      "duration_seconds": 4.41,
      "text": "Come in. Please sit. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 11.12,
      "end_seconds": 18.15,
      "duration_seconds": 7.03,
      "text": "Well, doctor, I'll sit in if that's okay, I know what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 19.37,
      "end_seconds": 23.41,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "That's fine, sit down. We'll go through it together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 25.17,
      "end_seconds": 34.58,
      "duration_seconds": 9.41,
      "text": "It's a burn on my left forearm, doctor. She didn't want to come, but I insisted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 35.55,
      "end_seconds": 39.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.92,
      "text": "So, how long has it been like this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 40.98,
      "end_seconds": 43.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.98,
      "text": "I've had it for two weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 44.78,
      "end_seconds": 50.31,
      "duration_seconds": 5.53,
      "text": "Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 51.3,
      "end_seconds": 66.65,
      "duration_seconds": 15.35,
      "text": "um, it settles a little with cool water i notice it more with clothes and touching it oh, and being worried about scarring that's been about the same, three days"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 68.33,
      "end_seconds": 74.67,
      "duration_seconds": 6.34,
      "text": "Have you had a burn on your left forearm before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 75.52,
      "end_seconds": 83.33,
      "duration_seconds": 7.81,
      "text": "Ah, yes, something like this happened last winter, and it went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 83.87,
      "end_seconds": 87.36,
      "duration_seconds": 3.49,
      "text": "Time for your numbers, if that's okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 97.94,
      "end_seconds": 100.18,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "Nearly done with the readings..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 109.88,
      "end_seconds": 119.66,
      "duration_seconds": 9.78,
      "text": "Okay: pulse is 80 beats a minute, pressure 126 over 80, respiratory rate 18, temp 36.4 degrees, oxygen saturation is 98 percent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 121.62,
      "end_seconds": 123.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "may I examine you now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 124.89,
      "end_seconds": 127.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.14,
      "text": "Raise your arm for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 137.42,
      "end_seconds": 146.28,
      "duration_seconds": 8.86,
      "text": "there is a five-centimetre area of redness with an intact blister on the left forearm, and it blanches and is painful"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 151.96,
      "end_seconds": 156.89,
      "duration_seconds": 4.93,
      "text": "All finished, thank you. Have you noticed trouble breathing or chemical exposure?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 157.83,
      "end_seconds": 163.64,
      "duration_seconds": 5.81,
      "text": "Sorry, uh, what was I saying, nope, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 164.73,
      "end_seconds": 168.83,
      "duration_seconds": 4.1,
      "text": "Did you get burn on the face or pus?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 170.79,
      "end_seconds": 176.6,
      "duration_seconds": 5.81,
      "text": "No burn on the face or pus, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 177.0,
      "end_seconds": 182.19,
      "duration_seconds": 5.19,
      "text": "Sure. Any pins and and needles or loss of strength anywhere?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 183.45,
      "end_seconds": 185.02,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "nothing odd there"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 185.88,
      "end_seconds": 191.01,
      "duration_seconds": 5.13,
      "text": "Tell me about your routine, work, habits, that sort of thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 191.57,
      "end_seconds": 206.42,
      "duration_seconds": 14.85,
      "text": "No, I share a house with my brother. I'm a plumber, lots of bending and kneeling. I grab fast food at lunch most days"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 206.98,
      "end_seconds": 210.66,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "Is there anything relevant on the family side?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 211.77,
      "end_seconds": 214.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "my grandfather had a stroke"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 214.98,
      "end_seconds": 218.36,
      "duration_seconds": 3.38,
      "text": "Any medical conditions, anything you've been treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 219.39,
      "end_seconds": 223.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "Yeah, no, nothing I can think of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 224.75,
      "end_seconds": 226.75,
      "duration_seconds": 2.0,
      "text": "any regular medication at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 228.55,
      "end_seconds": 233.31,
      "duration_seconds": 4.76,
      "text": "Let me think, no, I don't take any tablets."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 235.26,
      "end_seconds": 237.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "Have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 238.92,
      "end_seconds": 243.23,
      "duration_seconds": 4.31,
      "text": "no, um, I've never been operated on"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 252.05,
      "end_seconds": 255.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "are there any allergies I should be aware of?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 257.07,
      "end_seconds": 263.34,
      "duration_seconds": 6.27,
      "text": "Plasters. I come out in... well, a red itchy rash."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 274.53,
      "end_seconds": 281.59,
      "duration_seconds": 7.06,
      "text": "Taking everything into account, I'd lean towards a superficial partial-thickness burn. We shouldn't forget a deeper burn."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 286.69,
      "end_seconds": 288.37,
      "duration_seconds": 1.68,
      "text": "is this permanent?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 289.75,
      "end_seconds": 297.06,
      "duration_seconds": 7.31,
      "text": "nothing I've seen today points to an emergency it looks like a superficial partial-thickness burn"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 308.34,
      "end_seconds": 318.72,
      "duration_seconds": 10.38,
      "text": "what I'm giving you is paracetamol, 1 gram, every six hours if needed, for three days. That should help with burn pain"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 320.09,
      "end_seconds": 323.64,
      "duration_seconds": 3.55,
      "text": "Fine, you know, I'll begin it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 325.34,
      "end_seconds": 339.4,
      "duration_seconds": 14.06,
      "text": "cool the area under running water for twenty minutes and cover it with a non-stick dressing, and leave the blister alone. We'll catch up if it becomes more painful or smelly"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 340.15,
      "end_seconds": 343.72,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "I'll note it in my calendar."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 344.97,
      "end_seconds": 347.76,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "Have I covered everything you wanted?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 349.61,
      "end_seconds": 354.1,
      "duration_seconds": 4.49,
      "text": "Ah, okay, that makes sense. Thanks for explaining."
    }
  ]
}